  "summary_plain": "Forty-two printed regions on eight systems. The piece opens in treble and bass with two sharps and a 3/4 sign, and the first region is a one-beat pickup. Four later clef glyphs are printed on the lower staff: treble in the middle of P008, bass in the middle of P009, treble in the middle of P016, and bass immediately before the double barline of P017, governing P018. System 4 reprints that treble clef at its left edge; it is not another change. A thin-thin double barline with no repeat dots separates the two-beat partial P017 from the one-beat pickup P018. The last region, P042, holds two quarter-note beats and closes with a thin-thick barline. Every system begins and ends with a barline, so no bar is split across a system break. No repeat, ending, meter change, or key change is printed. Title, dynamics, slurs, and the closing hairpin stay inside the crops; the page number, plate mark, and publisher line are not musical ink.",
